humanizer-voiceprint
=====================

This project is a fork and combination of three MIT-licensed works.

1. Base skill: blader/humanizer
   https://github.com/blader/humanizer
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen
   The skill body and all 33 AI-writing detection patterns originate here.
   The upstream LICENSE is preserved in this repository as LICENSE.

2. Voice-fingerprint and saved-profile mechanism: numen-tech/slopornot
   (the "agentic-humanizer" skill)
   https://github.com/numen-tech/slopornot
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen, Copyright (c) 2026 Thilak Rao
   The persistent preference profile and the one-time stylometric voice
   fingerprint design (storage layout, extraction schema, cache-by-hash,
   and the field set) are adapted from that project.

3. Writing-craft rules: Anbeeld/WRITING.md (the "writing" skill, v1.4.1)
   https://github.com/Anbeeld/WRITING.md
   MIT License, Copyright (c) Anbeeld
   references/writing-craft.md distills that project's editing-integrity
   guards, no-fabricated-humanity safeguards, formula watchlist additions,
   structural defaults, and long-form diagnostics.

Changes made in this fork:
   - Profile and voice machinery reworked into a single rewrite pass rather
     than the slopornot 5-pass scoring loop.
   - Ported to Windows/PowerShell. No macOS app dependency and no
     Slop or Not Pro detector/readability/cleanup backend.
   - Storage namespace changed to $HOME/.humanizer/ to avoid colliding with
     the slopornot plugin's $HOME/.agentic-humanizer/.

